# Keep the build context small and the image free of state and secrets.

# ── Runtime STATE — comes from RDS and the EFS volume, never the image ──
# Relational state lives in RDS Postgres (NXR_DATABASE_URL); blobs come from the volume
# NXR_DATA_DIR points at. These .db files are the local-dev SQLite fallback, and baking
# them in doesn't just waste layers: if NXR_DATABASE_URL were ever missing, the container
# would present a stale committed twins.db as the live twin registry, silently reverting
# every twin a user created.
nextxr-ontology/data/
**/*.db
**/*.db-journal
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm

# ── Secrets ──
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key

# ── Local dev / build noise ──
.git/
.gitignore
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
node_modules/
frontend/node_modules/
# The federated UI is published to S3/CloudFront by CI, not shipped in the API image.
frontend/dist/
apps/*/frontend/node_modules/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.log

# ── Docs / non-runtime ──
# Deliberately NOT excluding *.glb / *.png globally: the backend ships packaged assets
# (packs/, imports/) and a blanket asset exclusion would strip them out of the image in a
# way that only shows up at runtime as a 404.
*.md
docs/
*.html
*.docx
